@template playful
// ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.3 item 26: crew comment when you wear dirty clothes. clothes.remark: yesterday's clothes
// (flag:clothes.stale); clothes.grubby: a grubby uniform (flag:clothes.grubby, AC3). Bubbles, 60 characters or fewer.
// Kind, never mean: the joke is on the clothes, not on you.
== clothes.remark
? flag:clothes.stale
- Day two of the same shirt! Going for a record?   #funny
- That shirt's back! Missed it. Didn't miss it.   #funny
? flag:clothes.stale tier>=friend
- Race you to the laundry. Loser folds.   #warm
== clothes.grubby
? flag:clothes.grubby
- Ooh, oil camouflage! Very stealthy. Not really.   #funny
- Ten points for the grime. Minus ten for the smell.   #funny
? flag:clothes.grubby tier>=friend
- Change, then come back. I want the whole story.   #warm

// ---- ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.5 item 5: more lines for the chat card's opener (greet, near), so a tap doesn't repeat.
// Heard after a person's own lines are used up (FX13's no-repeat). {hi}, {nick} and {me} are the speaker's own words.
== greet
- {hi}! Tag. You're it. No take-backs.
- {hi}, {nick}! Bet you can't guess what I've been doing.
- Ooh, it's you! Quick, look busy. Too late.
- {hi}! Rate my day out of ten. I'll go first: seven.
- {hi}! I was just about to do something silly.
- Hey! You owe me a rematch. Of something.
- {hi}! You're just in time for nothing at all!
- {hi}! New rule: everyone says hello twice. Hello. Hello.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {nick}! My favourite rival! Sort of rival.
- {hi}! Bet I can beat you to the lift. Later.
? time:morning
- Morning! I've already won breakfast. Don't ask how.
? time:evening
- Evening! Who's up for something daft?
== near
- Watch this. Okay, don't. It's going wrong.
- {room}! Best room. Today. Ask me tomorrow.
- I'm racing myself. I'm winning. And losing.
- Can you do this one-handed? I can. Nearly.
- I've given this a name. It doesn't like it.
- Ten seconds. Nine. Okay, a bit longer.
- Shh. I'm being very serious. See?
- Help me with this and I'll owe you a biscuit.
